# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Official inputs, GT and per-frame results stay local regardless of repository visibility.
#
# Everything below either is a private asset, would leak the answer, or is generated output. The
# history of this repo is new, so anything committed once is committed forever -- when in doubt,
# add it here first and take it out later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- private ground truth ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# All official ground truth is excluded from this development handoff.
# These legacy filename patterns are retained alongside whole-directory exclusions below.
*_possession_gt.csv
*_possession_gt_meta.json
*_possession_gt_reference.csv
possession_by_frame.pkl

# -- submissions -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any file in results/ is a set of labels for the whole match. A perfect one is a copy of the
# ground truth, so the folder ships empty and stays that way.
evaluation/results/*.csv

# ...with one deliberate exception. The baselines are computed from the ATD alone -- the same ATD
# every enrolled participant has -- and never read a ground truth of any kind, so they carry no
# information about the answer. They ship so that a fresh clone has something real to score.
!evaluation/results/baseline_*.csv
evaluation/reports/
evaluation/scoreboard.csv

# -- gated data --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ is committed empty, with only its README, so the folder participants are told to unpack
# into actually exists in a fresh clone. Everything they put in it stays out of git.
data/*
!data/README.md

*.mp4
*.gzip
*.pl3container

# -- internal documents ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OVERVIEW.md -- the institutional description of the competition -- IS committed. It is the only
# place that explains why the format changed from 2026, and a document like that circulating by
# email is exactly the artifact README.md's "anything you were sent earlier is superseded" line
# exists to prevent. Versioned next to what it describes, it cannot drift out of sight.
#
# The 2026 edition's documents were moved to ../mtah2027-organizers/archive-2026/ -- they describe
# a different competition and belong with the organiser tooling, not in this repository.
#
# *.pdf stays as insurance: internal decks and proposals have a habit of landing in the working
# tree, and this repository is public.
*.pdf

# Organiser tooling lives in ../mtah2027-organizers, outside this repository. This line is
# insurance against it being recreated in here by habit.
organizers/

# -- editors and build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store

# External-only prepared data, reports and per-frame targets (never source).
/external_artifacts/*

# Operator-only official inference output. Agents must not inspect this directory.
local_official_artifacts/

# Project-local execution environment, package cache and temporary fixtures.
runtime/

# User-acquired external SoccerTrack payloads; provenance summaries live in docs/.
/Soccertrack V2/


